,316],[125,933],[80,999],[567,630],[28,983],[910,347],[34,958],[49,898],[625,650],[39,929],[23,562],[167,939],[65,871],[111,875],[368,238],[595,669],[804,570],[152,984],[165,968],[647,578],[534,646],[6,1003],[686,638],[78,851],[580,477],[609,457],[527,913],[619,440],[105,987],[731,907],[118,855],[648,445],[139,1000],[181,954],[861,704],[27,861],[17,896],[35,905],[89,829],[549,915],[160,778],[450,888],[752,909],[139,940],[194,941],[438,207],[128,838],[509,908],[156,921],[68,966],[433,882],[713,901],[566,336],[597,452],[639,879],[17,844],[31,891],[656,543],[610,468],[550,656],[170,912],[124,957],[655,881],[682,489],[101,816],[609,679],[15,992],[4,890],[55,928],[205,929],[727,555],[48,955],[713,513],[122,974],[24,881],[591,569],[761,437],[112,803],[185,902],[135,825],[124,790],[146,813],[635,586],[139,779],[245,894],[607,540],[158,798],[215,918],[612,449],[790,509],[10,825],[498,600],[44,980],[199,901],[133,806],[302,288],[125,1003],[34,257],[775,542],[576,602],[18,684],[535,558],[574,581],[229,909],[114,981],[3,191],[573,484],[105,1005],[636,619],[630,869],[113,845],[604,474],[671,417],[227,901],[3,810],[101,836],[2,865],[203,912],[165,931],[192,930],[380,240],[107,964],[44,875],[227,888],[179,921],[144,794],[783,438],[767,601],[764,564],[758,596],[203,920],[131,817],[602,328],[752,590],[834,538],[819,539],[564,379],[801,525],[609,651],[607,655],[121,809],[121,830],[254,674],[912,419],[922,409],[644,384],[16,386]]}},"text":{"4":"Bodie had a soft little voice, and he did not talk very much. But his crayons always had a lot to say. Scritch-scratch! A long-neck dinosaur. Scritch-scratch! A volcano puffing a cloud. Dad peeked over his shoulder. \u201cWow,\u201d he said. \u201cDinosaurs!\u201d","24":"\u201cWould you like to see Dino Valley?\u201d asked Mossy. She laid her long tail on the ground like a slide. Pip scrambled up first. Bodie climbed after him, holding on tight. Then Mossy stood up, slowly and carefully. Up, up, UP! Now Bodie could see everything!","26":"Down by the river, a Triceratops family was playing in a mud pool. The baby rolled over and over. SPLISH! SPLOSH! Then she flicked her tail and splashed her mom. SPLAT! \u201cMud keeps their skin cool,\u201d said Pip. Bodie laughed. It looked like fun.","30":"Swoosh! Three Pteranodons glided over their heads on big, wide wings. Round and round they flew, high above the trees. \u201cThey\u2019re the best flyers in the valley,\u201d said Pip. One of them swooped low and dipped a wing at Bodie, like a wave. Bodie waved back.","32":"Next, they went to see Old Puff, the sleepy volcano. He sat far away, at the very edge of the valley. Puff\u2026 puff\u2026 went the little round clouds. \u201cOld Puff has been asleep for a thousand years,\u201d said Mossy. \u201cHe only snores clouds.\u201d Bodie giggled."}}